-- title:
--   Regularity of jmatĥ or its inverse at centred Igusa data, q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=2$ and a level $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q\in A.\mathrm{nonunits}$, and a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'$ (rational affine geometric places whose value of the geometric $j$-generator lies in the supersingular set). Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and fix a constant reduction $R₀$ of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ whose residue map computes coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ ($hR₀$); an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$; an index $\zeta\in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$; and two families of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. The Igusa family is subject to the explicit description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ by quotients of Laurent series over $A$ with nonzero reduction, transitivity of $\Gamma_0(M')$ on lines via pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$, injectivity, and permutation of the family by every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; the supersingular family is subject to contracting to $A$ on constants, to a compatibility clause expressing membership and residue values through $R₀$ and the evaluation of the corresponding place at the place-integral elements regular along $\hat\jmath$, to invariance under all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and to the existence for each $s$ of an element $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$. Descent data: a subfield $K₀\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over which $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is algebraic with $\pi\in K₀$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A₀$ with an injective local ring map $\iota:A₀\to A$ whose image is $A\cap K₀$, with surjective composite to $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and a generator $\varpi₀$ of the maximal ideal of $A₀$ with $\iota(\varpi₀)=\pi$; the subfield $F₀\subseteq\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K₀$, which contains the element $\hat\jmath$ obtained from $\mathrm{jq}$ by coefficient extension; and an $A₀$-algebra structure on $F₀$ compatible with $\iota$. Finally fix a line $\ell$, a valuation subring $V$ of $F₀$ contained in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and properly so (some element of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)\cap F₀$ lies outside $V$), and an $A₀$-subalgebra $B\subseteq F₀$ with a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$, such that $B$ is finitely generated, integrally closed in $F₀$ with $F₀$ as its field of fractions, every non-maximal prime containing $\varpi₀ B$ is minimal over $\varpi₀ B$, every nonzero prime not containing $\varpi₀ B$ has valuation-ring localisation, the only line $\ell'$ with $B\subseteq O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell')$ is $\ell$, no $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains $B$, $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)\cap F₀$ is the localisation of $B$ at some prime and equally at every minimal prime over $\varpi₀ B$, $B\subseteq V$, and $\mathfrak m$ is the contraction of the nonunits of $V$; assume moreover that some image of $\hat\jmath$ under the subgroup of automorphisms of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ lies in $B$ together with, or alternatively its inverse lies in $B$. The conclusion is that $\hat\jmath$ or $\hat\jmath^{-1}$ lies in the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m$: there are $b,c\in B$ with $c\notin\mathfrak m$ and $\hat\jmath\,c=b$, or there are such $b,c$ with $\hat\jmath^{-1}c=b$.
--
--   This is the local regularity step on the Igusa branch of the semistable covering construction for full level $q^2M'$: at a centred good datum $(B,\mathfrak m)$ refining the Igusa valuation ring attached to a line $\ell$, carrying a level translate of the modular invariant $\hat\jmath$ or of its inverse, one of $\hat\jmath$, $\hat\jmath^{-1}$ is already regular at the centre. It is the $q=2$ case, with the hypothesis $q=2$ replacing the condition $q\ge 5$ of the companion statement, and it feeds the construction of a formally smooth centred subalgebra on the same branch.
